  "source_text": "The initial form says No blackouts, but during further questioning the driver reports a blackout while queuing in the heat six weeks ago and describes a second collapse the following week; he recovered quickly, says someone suggested a faint, and has not been told by a treating clinician that either event was definitively vasovagal syncope.\r\n\r\nHe asks whether heat would count as a provoking factor, yet one episode apparently occurred indoors and the witness is unavailable; investigations have started but no final mechanism, specialist opinion or reliable long-term event-free interval is documented, and the two different dates must not be merged into a single event.\r\n",
